8. Termination.

You may not propagate or convey a covered work except as expressly
provided under this License. Any attempt otherwise to propagate or
convey a covered work is void, and will automatically terminate your
rights under this License (including any additional permissions
under section 7). However, if you cease all violation of this
License, then your license from a particular copyright holder is
reinstated (a) provisionally, unless and until the copyright holder
explicitly and finally terminates your license, and (b) permanently,
if the copyright holder fails to notify you of the termination by
some reasonable means prior to 60 days after the cessation.

Moreover, your license from a particular copyright holder is
reinstated permanently if the copyright holder notifies you of the
termination by some reasonable means, you cease all violation of this
License, and you cease all violation of this License for 30 days
after the notification.

Termination of your rights under this License does not terminate
the licenses of other parties who have received copies or rights
from you under this License. If your rights have been terminated
and not permanently reinstated, you do not have the right to
propagate or convey covered works under this License.

